      "rkaf:assertsValue": {
        "@value": "In a case in which a worker is injured or becomes ill on the day before scheduled time off such as a holiday, a planned vacation, or a temporary plant closing, you need to record a case of this type only if you receive information from a physician or other licensed health care professional indicating that the employee should not have worked, or should have performed only restricted work, during the scheduled time off; if so, you must record the injury or illness as a case with days away from work or restricted work, and enter the day counts, as appropriate.",
