      "skos:definition": {
        "en": "“Medical treatment” means the management and care of a patient to combat disease or disorder; for the purposes of part 1904, medical treatment does not include: (A) visits to a physician or other licensed health care professional solely for observation or counseling; (B) the conduct of diagnostic procedures, such as x-rays and blood tests, including the administration of prescription medications used solely for diagnostic purposes (e.g., eye drops to dilate pupils); or (C) “first aid” as defined in paragraph (b)(5)(ii) of this section."
      },
